{"term":"obvious","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7dd97f02b9b9f7865d","definition":"Easily discovered, seen, or understood; self-explanatory.","example":"Carried somehow, somewhither, for some reason, on these surging floods, were these travelers, of errand not wholly obvious to their fellows, yet of such sort as to call into query alike the nature of their errand and their own relations. It is easily earned repetition to state that Josephine St. Auban's was a presence not to be concealed.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["apparent","arrant","undoubted","glaring","bait","blatant","clear","clear as a bell","clear as day","clear cut","conspicuous","crystal clear","cut and dried","decided","elucidate","evident","eyely","intuitive","manifest","notable","noticeable","obvious","open-and-shut","ostensible","palpable","patent","plain","plain as a haystack","plain as a pikestaff","plain as day","plain as Dunstable highway","plain as porridge","plain as print","plain as Salisbury","plain as the nose on one's face","prima facie","res ipsa loquitur","splendent","straightforward","undissembled"],"antonyms":["clear as mud","inconspicuous","inevident","nonevident","muddied","muddled","non-obvious","nonobvious","opaque","subtle","unclear","unobvious","unevident"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obvious#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈɑb.vi.əs/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/ba/En-us-obvious.ogg/En-us-obvious.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":[]}